Z||000000||Indy-2M4||12-02-2001||10:52 AM||||Can someone tell me how you can take one image and paste it with another like I see on some of the sigs. Like Roger has Britny on his car. I have played with a couple of free photo editing programs and they don't have that option. I can't afford PhotoShop, but was wondering if you knew of a free or cheaper prgm that would let me do this  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"><BR>Thank You in advance,<BR>Kathy<P>------------------<BR>Kathy<BR>http:\\sofa.iwarp.com<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Indy_Sig2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||maryjane||12-02-2001||11:04 AM||||The scanner software that came with my scanner will do it. Paperport. Not nearly as good or easy as photoshop. Maybe the imaging program that comes on the windows cd? Wangsamp, I think it is. I never tried to use it much. Sorry, that's all my meager suggestions.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Jake_Dragon||12-02-2001||11:52 AM||||If you copy just what you want to the clip board it should work with most photo software.<BR>It will not look as good that's why Photoshop cost so much.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cheever3000||12-02-2001||12:11 PM||||I bought MS-PictureIt for my wife to use in her teacher projects, but I'm the only one who uses it!  It was between $50-$60 a year ago.  It's okay, but DO NOT use it for a website designer.  It came with NO printed instructions, everything is on the screen.  <P>What I do is make a cut-out then add it to a collage.  You choose what things in the collage go in front or behind the other things, and resize parts or rotate them, add text, all that stuff.  Then save it as a JPEG file and choose the size.  That's it.<P><BR>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Cheever_gold_sig.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by Cheever3000 (edited 12-02-2001).]||||reg||1
